WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.894
We know that Insidious's KeyFace demon has been around haunting the cell blocks

00:00:02.932 --> 00:00:06.458
of Dewbend State Penitentiary since at least 1953, but it's likely

00:00:06.474 --> 00:00:08.590
that his history goes back much deeper than that.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.046
As a child, psychic medium Elise Rainier encountered spirits of many who had

00:00:12.068 --> 00:00:14.394
died in the prison, but stuck around to haunt the place and the grounds

00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:15.246
surrounding it.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.446
-[Elise] There's so many spirits in this house, it's hard to tell the good from the evil.

00:00:18.468 --> 00:00:20.698
-[Elise] A lot of people died in that prison.

00:00:20.794 --> 00:00:23.354
Part of the reason there are so many spirits has to do with the execution

00:00:23.402 --> 00:00:24.902
site being located on property.

00:00:24.996 --> 00:00:28.246
Dewbend is most likely a stand in for a real prison penitentiary of New Mexico,

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:31.926
which opened in 1885 and contained a now defunct gas chamber for executions, 

00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:34.914
which, along with other incidents, gave the place a reputation

00:00:34.962 --> 00:00:35.762
of being haunted.

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:40.254
So it's likely that this is around the time KeyFace first started showing up, the late 1800s.

00:00:40.254 --> 00:00:43.799
To learn why this evil creature came to develop this terrifying look,

00:00:43.799 --> 00:00:46.234
where he fits into the hierarchy of Insidious entities and

00:00:46.272 --> 00:00:47.910
what this character truly represents.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.054
Stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:52.430
This video is sponsored by Factor.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:58.223
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.950
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.118
I'm gonna need everyone to turn around, please, and put your hands on the wall.

00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:06.206
Now, where did I put that whoopin' stick?

00:01:06.228 --> 00:01:09.066
In today's video, I am analyzing the antagonist of Insidious: The Last Key,

00:01:09.098 --> 00:01:10.602
which is the fourth chapter of the Insidious franchise.

00:01:10.666 --> 00:01:13.902
They call him KeyFace, which doesn't really make sense to me.

00:01:13.956 --> 00:01:16.390
Clearly, the keys are on his his fingers, not his face.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.806
Maybe they were trying to name this character in such a way that it would

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:22.082
remind people of Red Face, the poster boy of Insidious antagonist.

00:01:22.146 --> 00:01:25.046
Or maybe it has something to do with this early piece of concept art where

00:01:25.068 --> 00:01:28.354
the skin around his nose and mouth is absent, forming a kind of lock shape.

00:01:28.402 --> 00:01:32.317
But that does come with its own question, why wouldn't they just call him Lock Face? 

00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:35.638
But etymology aside, KeyFace was played by Javier Botet,

00:01:35.644 --> 00:01:38.966
who is known for his roles as lanky disjointed horror creatures like the Leper in IT,

00:01:38.988 --> 00:01:42.394
The Crooked Man in the Conjuring 2, and The Big Toe Monster in

00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:44.938
Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark, all of which are side villains.

00:01:44.954 --> 00:01:47.614
So it's nice to finally get to talk about one of his roles as the main bad guy.

00:01:47.652 --> 00:01:50.986
But to fully understand why this demon haunted and disturbed the ghost

00:01:51.018 --> 00:01:54.226
hunting hero Elise Rainier more than any other, we've got to take it back to

00:01:54.248 --> 00:01:57.090
his earliest victims at the Dewbend Penitentiary.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.574
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:05.266
KeyFace, like other demons of Insidious lore, takes on an appearance to

00:02:05.288 --> 00:02:06.942
appeal to those that he's trying to capture.

00:02:07.006 --> 00:02:09.998
I've previously analyzed other entities and discussed how their form factor

00:02:10.014 --> 00:02:12.274
is meant to lure their victims into The Further.

00:02:12.322 --> 00:02:15.238
Insidious director James Wan stated that The Red Face Demon was originally meant to

00:02:15.244 --> 00:02:18.498
lure curious children in with his bright colors and almost carnivalesque appearance.

00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:21.254
The Man Who Can't Breathe, from Insidious: Chapter 3,

00:02:21.292 --> 00:02:24.598
appeared as a sickly man in order to garner sympathy from victims and remind

00:02:24.614 --> 00:02:27.258
them of someone they know who had suffered, which is why Quinn Brenner lets

00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:29.338
her guard down around the demon after losing her mom.

00:02:29.424 --> 00:02:31.990
KeyFace's victims are all prisoners at the penitentiary;

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.098
His goal is to drag them into an even worse kind of captivity in the

00:02:35.104 --> 00:02:37.482
confines of the purgatory realm known as The Further.

00:02:37.546 --> 00:02:40.286
He appeals to them with his appearance by taking a form that teases the

00:02:40.308 --> 00:02:41.114
promise of freedom.

00:02:41.162 --> 00:02:43.946
With his keys for fingers, he almost looks like he could be a mischievous

00:02:43.978 --> 00:02:45.550
spirit who could let the prisoners out.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.042
He also has long, unkempt hair, a clear sign that he could be on their side,

00:02:49.096 --> 00:02:51.774
as opposed to the prison staff, who have strict requirements to maintain

00:02:51.822 --> 00:02:53.438
short, neatly groomed hairstyles.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:57.202
KeyFace was first granted access to the real world in September of 1953,

00:02:57.256 --> 00:03:00.126
when Elise Rainier, daughter of the prison's assistant warden, Gerald Rainier,

00:03:00.158 --> 00:03:02.946
is locked in the basement as punishment for using her psychic

00:03:02.978 --> 00:03:05.398
abilities to communicate with one of the many ghosts on the property.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:08.406
KeyFace uses a childlike voice to get her attention and shines a light

00:03:08.428 --> 00:03:10.882
through the keyhole of the door in the basement to try to quell her fear.

00:03:10.946 --> 00:03:14.134
Each demonic entity in The Further resides behind a red door, but since

00:03:14.172 --> 00:03:17.286
Elise is a medium, she can see the door in the real world, just as she can

00:03:17.308 --> 00:03:18.758
often see spirits in her world.

00:03:18.844 --> 00:03:22.078
KeyFace uses the voice to tell her to open this door with a key hanging on the wall,

00:03:22.084 --> 00:03:24.958
and explains that she's the only one that can help open all the doors.

00:03:24.964 --> 00:03:27.998
This is because Elise's father and brother clearly don't have the

00:03:28.004 --> 00:03:31.226
same ability that she does, and her mom, if she possesses any psychic ability,

00:03:31.258 --> 00:03:34.126
is afraid to use it, and probably mature enough to know better than

00:03:34.148 --> 00:03:35.338
to help a strange voice.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.466
However, when Elise unlocks the door, it spits out the Key, which now takes

00:03:38.488 --> 00:03:39.662
on a fleshy appearance.

00:03:39.726 --> 00:03:43.522
Elise watches in horror as KeyFace reaches out and the Key reattaches itself

00:03:43.576 --> 00:03:44.654
as one of his fingers.

00:03:44.702 --> 00:03:47.858
We see sparks as KeyFace touches the doorknob, which I'll explain in a

00:03:47.864 --> 00:03:48.296
little bit.

00:03:48.296 --> 00:03:51.714
His newfound access to the real world also allows Elise to enter The Further

00:03:51.762 --> 00:03:54.662
for the first time, causing her eyes to roll back in her head as the entire

00:03:54.716 --> 00:03:55.602
house shakes.

00:03:55.666 --> 00:03:58.434
When her mother comes down to respond to the commotion, she finds Elise

00:03:58.482 --> 00:04:01.398
convulsing and hyperventilating in the corner, and KeyFace influences a

00:04:01.404 --> 00:04:04.262
loose wire to wrap around her neck and hangs her where she stands.

00:04:04.326 --> 00:04:05.046
I don't know if Mrs. Rainier

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.946
had the same abilities as Elise, but if she did, I can see why

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:09.818
KeyFace wanted to get rid of her first.

00:04:09.904 --> 00:04:13.622
Her death causes the already abusive father, Gerald, to become even worse,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:17.198
which is exactly what KeyFace wants, because he literally thrives off of it.

00:04:17.284 --> 00:04:19.230
-[Elise] Fear and pain is what feeds them.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.062
Over the next 8 years, he would use that fear and pain to control

00:04:22.116 --> 00:04:23.194
Gerald's actions.

00:04:23.322 --> 00:04:25.840
-[Elise] Daddy doesn't mean it when he yells at me.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.270
-[Elise] He's scared of the man with the keys.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.942
-[Elise] He's the one controlling it all.

00:04:32.996 --> 00:04:34.962
-[Elise] He is the one who opens all the doors.

00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:38.146
In Insidious: Chapter 3, Elise explains that there are two types of demons

00:04:38.178 --> 00:04:40.966
those who want to possess the bodies of the living, like Red Face, and those

00:04:40.988 --> 00:04:43.638
who just want the souls of the living to join it in the shadows,

00:04:43.644 --> 00:04:44.642
like The Man Who Can't Breathe.

00:04:44.706 --> 00:04:47.606
Based on the fact that KeyFace operates out of a prison block and aims to

00:04:47.628 --> 00:04:50.182
capture as many people as possible, he seems to fall into the second category.

00:04:50.236 --> 00:04:53.786
KeyFace excels at controlling their actions, using their fear of

00:04:53.808 --> 00:04:55.226
him to make them do what he wants.

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:58.614
After Elise lets him into the world of the living, he forces Elise's father

00:04:58.662 --> 00:05:01.898
to become a kidnapper, and he secretly takes several women as prisoners in

00:05:01.904 --> 00:05:03.142
the extra room in his basement.

00:05:03.206 --> 00:05:06.286
After killing them, they become permanent prisoners when KeyFace traps their

00:05:06.308 --> 00:05:07.130
souls in The Further.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:09.022
So there are many layers at play here.

00:05:09.076 --> 00:05:12.798
Gerald works at a prison, keeps prisoners at home, and is a prisoner of the

00:05:12.804 --> 00:05:13.950
demon's control over him.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.826
Later, the suitcases of the women he kidnapped are discovered in an air duct

00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:17.482
in the basement.

00:05:17.546 --> 00:05:20.586
The 6th and presumably final victim was a waitress named Anna.

00:05:20.618 --> 00:05:23.838
In the early 1960s, she used a loose nail to escape from the room she was

00:05:23.844 --> 00:05:27.610
captive in and made it upstairs where she came face to face with a now teenage Elise.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:31.906
Only problem was, Elise was so used to seeing ghosts, and Anna, dirty, pale

00:05:31.938 --> 00:05:35.122
and malnourished from her time in captivity, kind of looked a bit ghastly

00:05:35.186 --> 00:05:37.090
like me after a long editing session.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:37.974
Because of this, Mr. Rainier

00:05:38.012 --> 00:05:40.886
was able to gaslight his daughter into thinking that Anna was just

00:05:40.908 --> 00:05:41.506
another ghost.

00:05:41.538 --> 00:05:44.090
And this leads to a fight where Elise runs away from home.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.222
This allows Gerald to go back and kill Anna without being discovered.

00:05:47.286 --> 00:05:50.246
I'm not sure what Elise's brother, Christian, was doing at the time, but it's

00:05:50.278 --> 00:05:53.238
possible that he was distracted by his distress over his sister abandoning

00:05:53.254 --> 00:05:53.754
the family.

00:05:53.824 --> 00:05:56.926
At some point, when he was old enough, Christian got out himself, and with

00:05:56.948 --> 00:06:00.366
nobody left to torture, KeyFace took Gerald's life and he became a ghost in

00:06:00.388 --> 00:06:00.888
The Further.

00:06:00.906 --> 00:06:03.598
Historically, the ghosts of The Further tend to maintain the appearance of

00:06:03.604 --> 00:06:06.686
the age that they died at, and Gerald's ghost looks to be about 15 to 20

00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:08.542
years older than he was in 1953.

00:06:08.596 --> 00:06:12.526
So we can assume that KeyFace killed him in the 1960s or 1970s and took his

00:06:12.548 --> 00:06:13.962
ghost as one of his prisoners.

00:06:14.026 --> 00:06:18.114
The house sat vacant for about 40 years until a single man named Ted Garza

00:06:18.162 --> 00:06:20.886
dumped his life savings into buying the house, which turned out to be as

00:06:20.908 --> 00:06:23.794
poor of a personal choice as it was a poor real estate investment.

00:06:23.842 --> 00:06:27.510
As he became the next to be haunted by the demon known as KeyFace.

