00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.454
After making contact with the house's newest inhabitant, Ted Garza,

00:07:51.502 --> 00:07:54.626
KeyFace forces him to kidnap a nurse from nearby and lock her in the basement

00:07:54.648 --> 00:07:57.950
For 4 months, continuing the cycle of abduction that he started with Gerald.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.046
-[Elise] I think it made Ted Garza do what he did.

00:08:00.088 --> 00:08:03.494
But unlike Gerald, Ted seems slightly more resistant and tries to take

00:08:03.532 --> 00:08:05.590
action to get rid of the disturbance from his home.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:09.234
Eventually, in 2010, he considers calling Elise's company Spectral Sightings

00:08:09.282 --> 00:08:11.798
to investigate, which really shows how desperate he must have been.

00:08:11.884 --> 00:08:14.614
Bringing in ghost hunters would make it pretty likely that his prisoner

00:08:14.662 --> 00:08:15.462
would be discovered.

00:08:15.526 --> 00:08:18.666
Then again, if KeyFace was controlling him, maybe that's what he wanted to happen.

00:08:18.688 --> 00:08:22.186
Maybe bringing Elise back into the fold was part of the plan for

00:08:22.208 --> 00:08:24.458
KeyFace to finally imprison the one that got away.

00:08:24.544 --> 00:08:27.678
But in the 40-something years since Elise's departure, she's buried a lot of

00:08:27.684 --> 00:08:28.362
her old memories.

00:08:28.426 --> 00:08:31.114
Due to the trauma that she experienced from her father, she's essentially

00:08:31.162 --> 00:08:33.022
forgotten about KeyFace in her elder years.

00:08:33.076 --> 00:08:36.826
But as KeyFace takes a stronger and stronger hold on Ted Garza, Elise begins

00:08:36.858 --> 00:08:40.146
having nightmares about KeyFace again and sketches him inside of her book of seeing.

00:08:40.168 --> 00:08:42.654
These nightmares consist of scenes from her childhood.

00:08:42.702 --> 00:08:45.902
And as these memories slowly come back, she fills in more of the picture.

00:08:45.966 --> 00:08:49.254
After one nightmare about her childhood, she writes down, give me the key.

00:08:49.372 --> 00:08:50.982
-[Elise] The dreams are coming back, Warren. It just won’t go away, will it?

00:08:51.036 --> 00:08:55.078
Screenwriter Leigh Whannell expanded on how he created the demon

00:08:55.084 --> 00:08:58.440
as a manifestation for what Elise is going through.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:03.722
-[Leigh] The demon really represents the trauma that has affected Elise her whole life.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:08.794
-[Leigh] And this demon, who has keys for fingers, has the power to lock and

00:09:08.832 --> 00:09:11.626
-[Leigh] unlock these doors into Elise's past.

00:09:11.728 --> 00:09:14.874
I think if we read between the lines here, KeyFace is not just literally

00:09:14.922 --> 00:09:18.266
unlocking these portals in The Further, but the keys represent him unlocking

00:09:18.298 --> 00:09:20.042
memories that bring back up the trauma.

00:09:20.106 --> 00:09:23.466
In psychology, this is known as triggering, a stimulus that causes a painful

00:09:23.498 --> 00:09:24.570
memory to resurface.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:28.706
It could be a sound, sight, smell, any other sensory experience, or even

00:09:28.728 --> 00:09:29.550
another memory.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.542
The reason for this is because the brain is a literal neural network.

00:09:32.606 --> 00:09:35.806
So as one part of the brain gets fired up, it'll also activate the neurons

00:09:35.838 --> 00:09:36.850
connected to that part.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:40.354
Neuropsychologist Donald Hebb used the term neurons that fire together, wire together.

00:09:40.402 --> 00:09:43.202
The concept is often seen in children who have suffered abuse.

00:09:43.266 --> 00:09:46.646
Oftentimes, any physical contact, good or bad, will trigger a fight or

00:09:46.668 --> 00:09:49.090
flight response because it triggers memories of the abuse.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.006
At the beginning, Elise doesn't seem to fully remember everything that went down.

00:09:52.028 --> 00:09:54.854
But the trauma comes back to her through her dreams and eventually

00:09:54.902 --> 00:09:56.522
through revisiting her childhood home.

00:09:56.576 --> 00:10:00.022
A trauma victim might even refer to this process as unlocking old memories,

00:10:00.086 --> 00:10:02.490
much like how you might unlock memories in a video game.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.518
The first night at the old house, Elise stays in her old room, where most of

00:10:05.524 --> 00:10:08.894
the supernatural activity is focused and a ghostly figure sneaks up on her.

00:10:08.932 --> 00:10:11.290
But when she turns, she sees her dad's old uniform.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:14.158
I believe that this was KeyFace because when she goes to touch the set of

00:10:14.164 --> 00:10:17.406
keys in the jacket pocket, she gets a little static shock, just like what we

00:10:17.428 --> 00:10:19.582
saw when KeyFace touched the doorknob in her childhood.

00:10:19.646 --> 00:10:22.722
There are also other examples of KeyFace having a shock to the touch going forward.

00:10:22.776 --> 00:10:26.050
Like his other attributes, I think there's symbolism here as well.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.326
Static electricity can be built up when materials rub together, causing

00:10:29.358 --> 00:10:30.818
electrons to build up in an object.

00:10:30.904 --> 00:10:33.362
When you touch that object, you may get a static shock.

00:10:33.426 --> 00:10:36.198
You can't see the electrons when they're built up on the surface,

00:10:36.204 --> 00:10:37.794
but they are there waiting to be accessed.

00:10:37.842 --> 00:10:40.690
It's a lot like how Elise represses her painful childhood memories.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:44.214
But when she revisits the house and comes across KeyFace, the memories rush

00:10:44.262 --> 00:10:46.118
back and she's in for a painful shock.

00:10:46.214 --> 00:10:49.546
Eventually, Anna's ghost helps Elise discover Garza's human prisoner and

00:10:49.568 --> 00:10:50.822
save her while she's still alive.

00:10:50.886 --> 00:10:54.266
When Garza retaliates, one of Elise's employees, Specs, is forced to trap him

00:10:54.288 --> 00:10:56.590
under her bookcase, which ultimately ends up killing him.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.574
KeyFace needs a new target, and finds one

00:10:58.612 --> 00:11:02.878
When Elisa's nieces, no rhyme intended, Melissa and Imogen visit the house to

00:11:02.884 --> 00:11:05.834
help Christian search for a whistle given to him by his mom before she died.

00:11:05.882 --> 00:11:08.994
Melissa searches the basement and finds several rings of keys, but after

00:11:09.032 --> 00:11:11.682
seeing one of them move on their own, discovers that they're actually

00:11:11.736 --> 00:11:15.010
connected to the hand of a demon, who easily slaps her across the room,

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:15.918
drawing blood.

00:11:16.014 --> 00:11:19.106
Then, from another part of the basement, he crawls toward her and sticks the

00:11:19.128 --> 00:11:21.986
key extending from his index finger into her throat, allowing him to lock

00:11:22.018 --> 00:11:24.338
her vocal cords, effectively putting her on mute.

00:11:24.434 --> 00:11:27.654
Then he inserts another key into her chest and locks her heart as well,

00:11:27.692 --> 00:11:30.966
which effectively puts her into a coma in the real world and imprisons her

00:11:30.988 --> 00:11:31.922
spirits in The Further.

00:11:31.986 --> 00:11:35.306
It ties back to this sign, seen when Elise and company first arrive at her

00:11:35.328 --> 00:11:36.454
hometown in New Mexico.

00:11:36.502 --> 00:11:38.134
It says, welcome to FIVE KEYS.

00:11:38.182 --> 00:11:39.418
We'll unlock your heart.

00:11:39.504 --> 00:11:41.910
That's exactly what they'd have to do to save Melissa.

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:45.566
By what I assume is a crazy coincidence, the actress that plays Melissa is

00:11:45.588 --> 00:11:46.682
named Spencer Locke.

00:11:46.746 --> 00:11:49.946
Or maybe there was some subconscious association going on during the casting process.

00:11:49.978 --> 00:11:53.214
Anyway, she's transferred to the hospital, so Elise and Tucker

00:11:53.262 --> 00:11:56.014
continue to investigate and find the air duct containing the suitcases

00:11:56.062 --> 00:12:00.850
of all the abducted women. Only one of them contains some extra baggage.

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:07.730
This drags Elise into The Further, where she sees more scenes of her past

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:11.286
and risks, paradoxy, by speaking to her younger self, encouraging her to

00:12:11.308 --> 00:12:12.610
never be afraid of her ability.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:13.974
KeyFace doesn't like the two Elise's co-conspiring however,

00:12:14.012 --> 00:12:17.158
and attacks the older version from behind

00:12:17.244 --> 00:12:20.770
before putting her in a cage, which is in a jail cell, kind of redundant.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:24.010
She's one of many prisoners stretching back as far as the eye can see.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.546
This means KeyFace likely has more prisoners in the dark than

00:12:27.568 --> 00:12:29.158
The Man Who Can't Breathe and Red Face combined.

00:12:29.254 --> 00:12:31.738
Each cell is themed to an area relevant to that person.

00:12:31.824 --> 00:12:34.214
Elise's is her childhood room, where she was abused.

00:12:34.262 --> 00:12:37.134
Her father's cell is the room with the TV, where he spent all of his free time.

00:12:37.172 --> 00:12:40.926
KeyFace unlocks their cells, but instead of attacking them himself,

00:12:40.948 --> 00:12:44.554
He simply hands Elise her dad's old cane, hoping to see Elise's anger overcome

00:12:44.602 --> 00:12:46.538
her and get revenge on her abusive dad.

00:12:46.634 --> 00:12:49.598
Remember, fear and pain is what feeds him, which makes him more of a

00:12:49.604 --> 00:12:52.090
psychological horror than his red and blue counterparts.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.286
Insidious: The Last Key director, Adam Robitel, touched on this little bit

00:12:55.308 --> 00:12:56.530
in an interview with Collider.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:59.590
-[Adam] I really felt like if you're gonna make a movie about Elise's origin story,

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:00.994
-[Adam] she's sort of like a superhero.

00:13:01.042 --> 00:13:03.766
-[Adam] She's not really afraid of ghosts, so you need something that really, really

00:13:03.788 --> 00:13:04.422
-[Adam] scares her.

00:13:04.476 --> 00:13:06.818
-[Adam] How do you do that? Well, you play into her psychology.

00:13:06.914 --> 00:13:09.478
-[Adam] You play on the thing that she hates the most, which is this relationship

00:13:09.564 --> 00:13:10.418
-[Adam] with her father.

00:13:10.514 --> 00:13:13.786
At first, she falls for it and repeatedly whacks him with the cane, just as

00:13:13.808 --> 00:13:16.154
he once did to her, and we see the effect in real time.

00:13:16.192 --> 00:13:19.306
It seems to exhilarate KeyFace and maybe even give him some power.

00:13:19.408 --> 00:13:22.970
As Elise beats down Gerald, there's a quick intercut shot of Gerald in turn,

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.614
abusing Anna, the captured woman in the 1960s.

00:13:25.652 --> 00:13:28.638
The Further is a realm capable of connecting different points in time, so it

00:13:28.644 --> 00:13:32.126
seems to suggest that KeyFace is simply using Elise's rage and channeling it

00:13:32.148 --> 00:13:32.810
to her father.

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:36.154
That raises the question of how time travel works in this universe.

00:13:36.202 --> 00:13:39.234
It seems to be the Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban model,

00:13:39.272 --> 00:13:41.970
Where those who travel back in time have always traveled back in time.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.982
This means that they can't change their destiny.

00:13:44.046 --> 00:13:46.898
There are infinite versions of Elise scattered through different points in time

00:13:46.904 --> 00:13:48.830
and they will all follow the same path.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:52.518
Even when our Elise was a child, she still spoke to the older Elise in

00:13:52.524 --> 00:13:54.390
The Further, even though that had not happened yet.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:57.030
It seems to be that she forgets about this encounter over the years,

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.878
allowing it to happen at this point in time over and over again.

00:13:59.964 --> 00:14:03.518
We saw something similar happen in Insidious: Chapter 2, when Josh Lambert

00:14:03.554 --> 00:14:06.218
was the one to set off the burglar alarm in his house during the events of

00:14:06.224 --> 00:14:07.078
the first Insidious.

00:14:07.174 --> 00:14:10.586
The result of this is the dark truth that Elise's inability to control her

00:14:10.608 --> 00:14:14.026
rage resulted in the deaths of the waitress Anna in the past, and there's

00:14:14.058 --> 00:14:15.722
nothing she can do to change her destiny.

00:14:15.786 --> 00:14:19.278
However, she soon realizes that her hatred is feeding the demon, setting up

00:14:19.284 --> 00:14:22.080
a confrontation 57 years in the making.

00:14:22.248 --> 00:14:25.236
(IMPACT)

00:14:27.172 --> 00:14:30.866
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:35.266
After discovering Elise had, like Melissa, fallen into a coma,

00:14:35.288 --> 00:14:38.658
Elise's other niece, Imogen, revealed that she too has the ability to see

00:14:38.664 --> 00:14:40.482
the spirits and volunteer to venture into The Further herself

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:43.826
To hopefully rescue her distressed family members.

00:14:43.858 --> 00:14:46.598
She goes to KeyFace's lair beyond the Red Door, the cell block where he keeps

00:14:46.604 --> 00:14:49.250
all of his prisoners, and sees him slam Elise back into captivity.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.062
Then he sets his sights on Imogen.

00:14:51.126 --> 00:14:54.954
Although Elise is able to just telepathically free herself,

00:14:54.992 --> 00:14:56.182
I'm not sure why she didn't use this earlier.

00:14:56.246 --> 00:14:57.254
KeyFace reappears with both nieces now in captivity, 

00:14:57.302 --> 00:15:00.714
Elise offers to give herself up,

00:15:00.752 --> 00:15:04.758
bartering for the demon to let them go, but then KeyFace just brutally slaps

00:15:04.774 --> 00:15:05.610
her across the room.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.766
I actually kind of appreciate this guy for being the one demon in any of

00:15:08.788 --> 00:15:12.074
these 2010s paranormal horror movies that'll actually just smack his enemies

00:15:12.122 --> 00:15:13.262
instead of air eating them.

00:15:13.316 --> 00:15:16.186
Especially when you consider that The Last Key was directed by Adam Robitel,

00:15:16.218 --> 00:15:17.974
a former Paranormal Activity director.

00:15:18.042 --> 00:15:20.722
I imagine that getting slapped across the room is more painful too.

00:15:20.776 --> 00:15:23.534
I assume getting air yeeted feels something like a good launch coaster.

00:15:23.582 --> 00:15:25.550
It's shocking, but it's not really something that hurts.

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:28.862
Whereas getting smacked by KeyFace would be a lot like riding Green Lantern first flight,

00:15:28.926 --> 00:15:31.046
you're definitely going to be walking out of there with some bruises.

00:15:31.068 --> 00:15:33.894
And that's not the only damage that KeyFace dishes out.

00:15:33.932 --> 00:15:37.014
He stabs Melissa in the back, causing her to writhe and convulse in the real world,

00:15:37.052 --> 00:15:38.658
where she begins to flatline.

00:15:38.754 --> 00:15:41.814
Using some kind of speed ability, he tries to bum rush Elise, but to her surprise, 

00:15:41.852 --> 00:15:45.098
her father's ghost comes to her defense and KeyFace eliminates him

00:15:45.104 --> 00:15:47.910
with a single stab, causing him to just dissipate from The Further.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:51.206
After all this time of being afraid of KeyFace and caving into his evil demands,

00:15:51.238 --> 00:15:54.026
I'm not really sure what made Gerald finally stand up to his captor

00:15:54.048 --> 00:15:57.374
If I had to guess, he simply saw this as his best opportunity to escape.

00:15:57.412 --> 00:16:01.006
But perhaps he also felt guilty after seeing Elise take mercy on him

00:16:01.028 --> 00:16:02.878
and decided to actually help her out for once.

00:16:02.964 --> 00:16:06.314
However, he's only a minor setback for the powerful KeyFace, whose roar

00:16:06.362 --> 00:16:07.482
knocks Elise to the ground.

00:16:07.546 --> 00:16:10.846
He tries to do to her what he did to Melissa and Imogen by locking her vocal cords.

00:16:10.878 --> 00:16:14.146
But Imogen realizes there's one thing she can do without using her

00:16:14.168 --> 00:16:15.822
voice and tosses Elise the whistle.

00:16:15.886 --> 00:16:18.978
This whistle was once given to Christian as a way to call his mother if he

00:16:18.984 --> 00:16:19.790
was ever afraid.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:23.158
As the demon goes for her heart, elise stabs it in the face, giving her a

00:16:23.164 --> 00:16:26.754
moment's time to retrieve and sound the whistle. Just as it had in her youth,

00:16:26.802 --> 00:16:29.766
It summons her mother, who still lives in The Further as a spirit and

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:31.610
fearlessly confronts the monster.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.058
-[Mrs. Rainier] Hands off my little girl. 

00:16:33.136 --> 00:16:37.654
KeyFace charges, but Mrs. Rainier issues an explosion of light from her lantern

00:16:37.702 --> 00:16:39.062
to send the creature blasting off into the dark.

00:16:39.126 --> 00:16:42.186
And if you look closely, the attack seems to burn right through his body as well,

00:16:42.208 --> 00:16:45.058
Which seems to suggest that the ancient Key keeper of the

00:16:45.094 --> 00:16:47.678
Dewbend Penitentiary is defeated once and for all.

00:16:47.764 --> 00:16:50.826
It makes sense that this antagonist, who represents the trauma Elise

00:16:50.858 --> 00:16:53.886
incurred during her childhood, is destroyed shortly after the demise of Gerald,

00:16:53.908 --> 00:16:56.154
the one who physically dished out that trauma.

00:16:56.202 --> 00:16:59.554
And he's defeated by Elise's mom, the one person who always tried to stand

00:16:59.592 --> 00:17:01.198
up for Elise against her father.

00:17:01.294 --> 00:17:04.306
There's one thing I have to address because I know people are going to bring

00:17:04.328 --> 00:17:04.712
it up.

00:17:04.712 --> 00:17:08.126
In the Blu-ray special feature Unlocking the Five Keys, executive producer

00:17:08.158 --> 00:17:11.560
Bailey Conway Anglewicz offers a different account of KeyFace's history.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:16.946
-[Bailey] This is in Elise's childhood home, and it's a big house on the prison property.

00:17:16.978 --> 00:17:20.258
-[Bailey] Her father was the assistant warden of the prison.

00:17:20.354 --> 00:17:24.306
-[Bailey] KeyFace was a very old prisoner who was wronged,

00:17:24.418 --> 00:17:25.270
-[Bailey] and that's why he haunts this property.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:28.594
This isn't part of the movie itself, so I don't really consider it canon.

00:17:28.642 --> 00:17:30.602
And there are several problems with this statement.

00:17:30.666 --> 00:17:32.954
She says KeyFace was an old prisoner who was wronged.

00:17:33.002 --> 00:17:35.646
There's no evidence of that in the movie, and he's specifically referred to

00:17:35.668 --> 00:17:36.990
as a demon multiple times.

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:39.098
We know that demons are non human entities.

00:17:39.194 --> 00:17:41.918
If you saw My Man Who Can't Breathe video, you may remember that there was a

00:17:41.924 --> 00:17:43.594
similar mix up regarding that character.

00:17:43.642 --> 00:17:46.202
And Bailey Conway Anglewicz is the executive producer.

00:17:46.266 --> 00:17:49.166
While executive producer roles can vary in how involved they are, she's

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:52.094
essentially the person who funds the movie, so she may not be the definitive

00:17:52.142 --> 00:17:53.522
source on lore related stuff.

00:17:53.576 --> 00:17:55.810
I do appreciate that she has CZ in her name, though.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.738
Someone who is more definitive regarding Lore would be the writer Leigh Whannel,

00:17:58.754 --> 00:18:01.846
who clearly refers to both The Man Who Can't Breathe and KeyFace as demons.

00:18:01.868 --> 00:18:07.046
-[Leigh] The demon really represents the trauma that has affected Elise her whole life.

00:18:07.068 --> 00:18:10.454
And KeyFace really does seem to affect Elise in a much more

00:18:10.492 --> 00:18:13.174
personal way than even a more powerful demon like Red Face.

00:18:13.222 --> 00:18:16.326
When dealing with Red Face, she certainly seems intimidated and concerned,

00:18:16.358 --> 00:18:17.914
but with KeyFace, it's personal.

00:18:18.032 --> 00:18:21.306
In one deleted scene, the demon locks her in this room in her house, and she

00:18:21.328 --> 00:18:24.282
starts crying and feels helpless, turning her into the little girl once

00:18:24.336 --> 00:18:25.770
locked in the basement by her father.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:28.686
That's why I introduced KeyFace the way I did at the beginning of this video.

00:18:28.708 --> 00:18:32.298
Even if he doesn't possess the raw power of Red Face or the diverse

00:18:32.314 --> 00:18:35.066
subset of abilities as The Man Who Can't Breathe, it is KeyFace's

00:18:35.098 --> 00:18:38.270
psychological aspects that allowed him to haunt and disturb the usually

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.398
stoic hero more than any other.

00:18:40.484 --> 00:18:43.406
And if you haven't seen my analysis of those other Insidious spirits, check

00:18:43.428 --> 00:18:46.146
out that playlist on the left to see the history of all this universe's monsters.

00:18:46.178 --> 00:18:49.926
If you love horror, make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new

00:18:49.948 --> 00:18:50.870
horrors every week.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.534
Ring the death bell for all notifications, and I will see you in the next one.

00:18:54.572 --> 00:18:56.690
Assuming we both survive.

